  },
  "body": "This is part of https://github.com/w3c/webcomponents/issues/533. It introduces a new custom element state of \"failed\", which HTML will use on failed upgrades or failed parser-initiated element creation, to ensure that if a constructor fails, the element will not be upgraded in the future (i.e. the constructor will not be called again for that element).\n",
